Z||000000||lowCG||06-11-99||10:38 PM||||I've recently found what sounds to be a fairly decent,and well cared for '87 SE V-6 5sp.PW,PL,CC,for the paltry sum of $1,100.There was a catch though;I have to travel from one coast to the other to get it,and drive(fun)back again.Haven't had a Fiero for a couple years,want another,am currently not working,no obligations,so...<br>Then I hear from the current owners today,who said they "just had the ignition go bad"and took it to the shop where $600 was spent on various(brakes,cables,ignition)so the price has gone up.Sucks,but I'm going to offer $1400 if they can produce some pictures of a decent car.<br>What do you think? Good deal? Totally nuts?
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||06-11-99||11:00 PM||||No, I don't think your nuts. I have been looking for an 88 for some time and almost went to New Mexico to get an abused Formula for $1,600. Then i found an 88GT in California(I live in Utah) with tranny trouble for $2,200. I seriously considered it, but there was another 88GT in California that was $1,900 come to find out it was an 87GT. I started to think about traveling so far to find something I didn't want. Then one day I noticed an 88 coupe in my town. I wanted a GT or Formula but settled for the coupe(I plan to install my V6 from my other Fiero). If I ever find an 88GT or Formula for a good price again I may consider it.<p>BTW if anyone is interested in these cars I will give you the info you need and pictures
